  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 49a9dd75b14f64f43a98b9b523c7ac90, type: 3}
  m_Name: MarcyCubicle
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DialogueObject
  _concurrentDialogue:
  - Marcy and I dated once. I always thought having an office romance would be exciting,
    that we would sneak glances to each other and smile about secrets only we were
    privy to.
  - Instead, it was just awkward.
  - It was strange to run into someone I had just gone on a first date with the next
    morning during our briefing.
  - "It felt like we were invading each other\u2019s privacy."
  - "After she told me we couldn\u2019t keep seeing each other, we didn\u2019t talk
    much. We caught these little glimpses of each other\u2019s life during a brief
    vulnerability, and then nothing"
  - I know she would usually spend her mornings going on a run and watching the sunrise.
    I wonder if she did that today, if it felt different knowing it was the last
    time she would ever see the sun go up.
  - "I wish I\u2019d tried running in the morning. It\u2019s too late now.  "
  _characterName: You
  _nextDialogue: {fileID: 0}
  _choices: {fileID: 0}
